    caret_closure_enum_payload_binding_collection_gaps_2026_11_03, 1, "2026-11-10 enumerated the three classes as 22 concrete lambda/collection shapes driven through the pure-Simple HIR->MIR lowering (test/01_unit/compiler/50.mir/caret_closure_enum_payload_binding_collection_spec.spl). Red on release/1.0.0 tip: class 3 captured Dict d.get(k) inside a lifted lambda -> unresolved method call: get route=runtime-fallback owner= then cannot materialize lambda (lower_lambda_value_for_type loads every capture as a bare i64 word and never carried the parent MIR Dict/Array type or runtime_dict_locals/runtime_array_locals/runtime_elem_value_type markers). Fix: switch_operators_calls.spl capture-load block re-types Dict/Array captures with the source MIR type and copies the collection markers into the lift. Class 1 (Option param match / captured Option match) and class 2 (for-in over captured array) were red on the older 27e65c24371 tip and already green on the release tip; kept as prevention rows. Evidence: older tip 18/22 -> release tip 21/22 -> after fix 22/22; sibling lambda_lift_*_capture_scan specs unchanged. Native caret closure build not re-run (no native lane on this host); verification pending."
